#
# Counter-example for gmeow:ProjectionObjectConflationConstraint (gmeow:ProjectionObjectConflation,
# the semantic-topology ResultObjectConflation twin). The module authors this gate on
# gmeow:PreferenceOrder: a gmeow:PreferenceOrder wrapper must REFERENCE a raw math:Relation
# through gmeow:orderRelation, never itself be typed in the math: namespace. Here ex:order is
# typed BOTH gmeow:PreferenceOrder AND math:Relation — the auditable wrapper conflated with the
# pure mathematical referent. The ∀→¬∃ SPARQL constraint (matching the order's own rdf:type in
# the math: namespace) MUST reject it with shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding.
# The order correctly references a distinct raw math:Relation through gmeow:orderRelation, so the
# self-conflation is the sole violation.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/preference/tests/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

ex:rawRelation a math:Relation ; rdfs:label "the raw math:Relation the order should merely reference"@en .

# The DEFECT: the order wrapper IS ALSO a raw math: object (conflation).
ex:order a gmeow:PreferenceOrder , math:Relation ;      # <-- typed in the math: namespace
    rdfs:label "a preference order conflated with a raw math:Relation"@en ;
    gmeow:orderRelation ex:rawRelation .
